            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Shawn Chapple"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This marinade is delicious and I used it with a nice pork chop. I didn't have long to marinate this so I just baked it in the oven and let the sauce reduce and thicken. I substituted real ginger for the powder and honey for the molasses. I added some red pepper flakes for some heat. YUMMM!!! and quick and easy."
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "gmainwa"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Great for pork , chicken and shrimp. I used 1/2 C Sweet red wine (that's all I had), so I omitted the sugar and I added a heaping tablespoon if minced garlic...I could not get the molasses to combine so I heated the marinade in the microwave for about 25 seconds...that fixed it. Simple and fantastic. Thanks for sharing.",
            "datePublished": "2012-09-25T10:17:12.760Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "East Bay Adam"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I used this on a tri-tip and it turned out PERFECTLY! I marinated for 36 hours and the meat was so flavorful all the way through. Everybody raved about the flavor of the meat.",
            "datePublished": "2023-05-02T03:26:01.062Z"
          },
          {
